\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces End-to-end experimental pipeline, from labelled satellite imagery to a saved, comparable results file per combination of component, architecture and test set.}}{43}{figure.caption.28}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Augmentations applied to a single \textbf {Scum} clarifier from Cape Flats. Top row: the original image, followed by a horizontal flip, a rotation of $15^\circ $, and a random colour jitter, each applied on its own. Bottom row: four random outputs of the full augmentation pipeline (flip, rotation and colour jitter combined).}}{48}{figure.caption.30}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces The training loop used for every architecture: an epoch of training and development-set evaluation, a scheduler step, a checkpoint decision based on development loss, and a stopping check repeated every epoch until training ends.}}{60}{figure.caption.42}%
